sequenceDiagram
    %% Comments flow 3 of 4 — Posting a comment
    %% The main flow. Five renders per post; the optimistic row is on screen
    %% before the request is made.
    %% Participants map to:
    %%   SH  ios/CommentSheetView.swift
    %%   NV  ios/RNPdfViewer.swift (RNPdfView)
    %%   JS  src/components/PdfViewer.js
    %%   MS  src/screens/ManuscriptScreen.js
    %%   ST  src/stores/commentsStore.js
    %%   API src/services/commentsService.js
    autonumber
    actor R as Reader
    participant SH as CommentSheetView
    participant NV as RNPdfView
    participant JS as PdfViewer.js
    participant MS as ManuscriptScreen.js
    participant ST as commentsStore
    participant API as commentsService
    participant SRV as Server

    Note over R,SH: Sheet is already open on a .thread or a .draft

    R->>SH: tap send
    SH->>SH: trim body, guard on empty or submitting
    SH->>NV: commentSheet(didSubmit: body, parentId: replyTo?.id)
    SH->>SH: clear composer, replyTo = nil, render (1)
    Note over SH: Commits on the tap, not on the network

    NV->>NV: switch on sheet.target
    Note over NV: .thread pulls page/anchorText/bounds/fileHash<br/>off the resolved thread.<br/>.draft uses values captured at selection time
    NV->>NV: clearSelection on the PDF
    NV->>JS: onSubmitComment nativeEvent
    JS->>MS: onSubmitComment({page, anchorText, bounds, fileHash, parentId, body})

    MS->>MS: setSubmitting(true)
    MS->>NV: submitting = true
    NV->>SH: update then render (2)
    SH->>R: send button shows spinner, disabled

    MS->>ST: addComment({roomId, bookId, page, anchorText, anchorBounds, parentId, body, fileHash})

    ST->>ST: clientId = cmt_ base36 time + random
    ST->>ST: anchorKey = parentId ? null : "pending:" + clientId
    ST->>ST: build optimistic comment, pending=true, id=clientId

    alt reply, parentId set
        ST->>ST: append to that root's replies
    else comment on a passage that already has a thread
        ST->>ST: append to t.comments, matched on page + anchorText
    else brand-new passage
        ST->>ST: fabricate a thread with the client-invented anchorKey
    end

    ST-->>MS: byBook updated, synchronous set
    MS->>MS: nativeThreads useMemo
    MS->>NV: threads prop
    NV->>NV: re-parse, update scrubber ticks, scheduleOverlayRefresh
    NV->>SH: update then render (3)
    SH->>SH: target.resolve, draft matched on page + anchorText
    Note over SH: Same rule addComment used to place it,<br/>so they agree by construction
    SH->>R: comment visible, spinner in its actions row

    ST->>API: createComment(roomId, bookId, {..., clientId})
    API->>SRV: POST /room/{roomId}/book/{bookId}/comments

    alt 201 Created
        SRV-->>API: saved row + anchor.key
        API-->>ST: status, response
        ST->>ST: swap optimistic by clientId, pending=false
        ST->>ST: thread.anchorKey = response.anchor.key
        Note over ST: Server owns the anchor key. The client's<br/>"pending:..." key is replaced here
        ST-->>MS: byBook updated
        MS->>NV: threads prop
        NV->>SH: update then render (4)
        SH->>R: spinner gone, real id so likes work, real timestamp
        Note over SH: Survives the key swap because a draft<br/>tracks page + text, not the key
    else non-201 or network error
        SRV-->>API: error
        API-->>ST: failure
        ST->>ST: set pending=false, failed=true by clientId
        ST-->>MS: byBook updated
        MS->>NV: threads prop
        NV->>SH: update then render (4)
        SH->>R: row shows "Couldn't send, Retry"
        ST--xMS: rethrow
        MS->>R: showToast "Couldn't post that, tap retry on the comment"
        Note over MS: The sheet has already moved on,<br/>so the toast carries the news
    end

    MS->>MS: finally setSubmitting(false)
    MS->>NV: submitting = false
    NV->>SH: update then render (5)
    NV->>NV: debounced refreshOverlays fires
    NV->>R: highlight + gutter dot appear for the new thread
